---
import Check from '../Check.astro';
import Frame from '../Frame.astro';

// Shown through set:html because the bundle contains braces and quotes that Astro markup would parse.
const bundle = [
  '<span class="hd"># Incident inc_8f2k · production · Error · Open</span>',
  '<span class="hd">Release</span>   v41 (a1b2c3d — orders: add fulfillment status column) · previous v40 · config unchanged',
  '<span class="hd">Signals</span>',
  '  - Uptime check down · https://api.acme.com/health · 3/3 regions',
  '  - Application error · <span class="am">PrismaClientKnownRequestError: column "fulfillment_status" does not exist</span>',
  '    apiService · 214 occurrences · <span class="hi">api/src/orders/repository.ts:41</span> findMany → prisma.orders',
  '<span class="hd">Timeline</span>  18:01 deploy v41 · 18:04 alarm · 18:05 uptime down · 18:05 opened',
  '<span class="hd">Links</span>     logs · trace · deploy v41 · compare v40…v41   (scoped to this stage)',
  '<span class="hd">Protocol</span>  1. find the cause in the release diff   2. fix it and open a PR',
  '          3. verify with the same signals        4. <span class="hi">stacktape incidents:resolve --incidentId inc_8f2k</span>'
].join('\n');
---

<Frame url="<b>Claude Code</b> · acme-project" tag="your coding agent">
  <div class="sp-frame__body">
    <div class="sp-agent">
      <div class="sp-agent__msg">
        <span class="sp-agent__who sp-agent__who--you" aria-hidden="true">you</span>
        <span>Production is down, here are the details from Stacktape. Find the cause and open a PR.</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="sp-bundle" aria-label="Handoff bundle from Copy details for agent" set:html={bundle}></pre>
      <div class="sp-agent__msg">
        <span class="sp-agent__who" aria-hidden="true">ai</span>
        <span>
          <b>Found it.</b> a1b2c3d adds <code>fulfillment_status</code> through a Prisma migration, but the <code>afterDeploy</code> hook that runs
          <code>prisma migrate deploy</code> was skipped for this stage, so production never received the migration. The code reads a column the
          database does not have. I re-enabled the hook for production and applied the migration. Opening a pull request.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sp-pr">
        <Check kind="ok" label="merged" />
        <span>
          <b>#129 · production: run the migration hook after deploy</b>
          <span>approved by matus 18:11 · merged · deploying as v42 through the normal pipeline</span>
        </span>
        <span class="sp-chip sp-chip--live"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>v42 · 2m 40s</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Frame>
